out the season.\",\"Total sunshine hour rded from 1955.\",\"Climate change may refer to a specific area or the entire world.As a result of climate change, weather patterns may become less.\"],\"conclusion\":\"Overall, our findings show considerable variation between stations with decrease and increase precipitation trends at the annual, seasonal, and monthly scales, with major increasing trends primarily occurring in January, August, winter, and summer, and major declining trends primarily occurring in October and autumn.\",\"structured_summary\":[],\"paragraph_summaries\":[{\"paragraph_number\":1,\"section\":\"Abstract\",\"purpose\":\"Abstract\",\"main_idea\":\"Our findings show considerable variation between stations with decrease and increase precipitation trends at the annual, seasonal, and monthly scales, with major increasing trends primarily occurring in January, August, winter, and summer, and major declining trends primarily occurring in October and autumn.\",\"supporting_details\":[],\"keywords\":[],\"summary\":\"Our findings show considerable variation between stations with decrease and increase precipitation trends at the annual, seasonal, and monthly scales, with major increasing trends primarily occurring in January, August, winter, and summer, and major declining trends primarily occurring in October and autumn.\"}],\"excluded_sections\":[],\"readability\":{\"original_word_count\":8098,\"summary_word_count\":66,\"compression_percent\":99.2,\"estimated_reading_time_minutes\":1,\"estimated_source_reading_time_minutes\":41},\"summary_method\":{\"name\":\"General Adaptive Hybrid Summarization\",\"topic_component\":\"textrank_with_lsa_support\",\"redundancy_reduction\":\"mmr\",\"scoring_strategy\":\"adaptive_hybrid\",\"fallback_used\":false,\"pipeline\":[\"source_resolution\",\"text_extraction\",\"text_cleaning\",\"article_type_detection\",\"section_detection\",\"paragraph_boundary_preservation\",\"sentence_tokenization\",\"hybrid_sentence_scoring\",\"redundancy_aware_reranking\",\"lsa_fallback_when_needed\",\"paragraph_level_analysis\",\"mmr_redundancy_reduction\",\"structured_output_formatting\",\"summary_quality_validation\"],\"scoring_weights\":{\"graph_topic_rank\":0.26,\"tfidf_keyword_score\":0.18,\"title_similarity\":0.14,\"section_priority\":0.12,\"paragraph_position\":0.1,\"keyword_bonus\":0.1,\"entity_bonus\":0.07,\"global_position\":0.03,\"redundancy_penalty\":0.12,\"bad_length_penalty\":0.1,\"citation_noise_penalty\":0.08}},\"source_metadata\":{\"source_type\":\"pdf\",\"title\":\"Analysis of the climate change trend in Nanjing from 1951 to 2020\",\"article_type\":\"Academic\",\"article_type_key\":\"academic\",\"engine\":\"general_adaptive_hybrid\",\"scoring_strategy\":\"adaptive_hybrid\",\"original_word_count\":8098,\"cleaned_word_count\":8098,\"paragraph_count\":1,\"candidate_sentence_count\":385,\"fallback_used\":false}}', 'standard_paragraph', 'completed', NULL, '2026-05-09 09:25:23');
